|~ What is declared under `::keyword`: the refusal of its
   constructor, and the comparisons of keywords, which compare two
   keywords by their names in the one order. ~|

:keyword/construct
  |~~ Reads a keyword as itself. ~~|
  ::builtin{}

:keyword/PayloadNotKeywordError
  |~~ `::keyword` reads its payload as the keyword it is; a string
      becomes one by `keyword`.
  ~~|

:keyword/PayloadNotKeywordError/refusesAString
  |~~ A string payload is refused; `keyword` turns a string into one. ~~|
  ::law~(::keyword"k" !| [type /actualType] | eq [::keyword/PayloadNotKeywordError ::string])

:keyword/gt
  |~~ Whether the subject's name follows the name of the keyword the
      call gives.
  ~~|
  ::builtin{}

:keyword/gt/ordersByName
  |~~ `:b` follows `:a`. ~~|
  ::law~(:b | gt :a | eq true)

:keyword/gt/value
  |~~ The value the subject is compared with. ~~|
  ~(/0)

:keyword/gt/value/NotKeywordError
  |~~ The value compared is a keyword. ~~|
  ::holds~(is ::keyword)

:keyword/gt/answer
  |~~ Whether the subject comes after the value compared. ~~|
  ::boolean

:keyword/gte
  |~~ Whether the subject's name follows or equals the name of the
      keyword the call gives.
  ~~|
  ::builtin{}

:keyword/gte/holdsOfItself
  |~~ A keyword follows or equals itself. ~~|
  ::law~(:b | gte :b | eq true)

:keyword/gte/ordersByName
  |~~ `:b` follows `:a`. ~~|
  ::law~(:b | gte :a | eq true)

:keyword/gte/value
  |~~ The value the subject is compared with. ~~|
  ~(/0)

:keyword/gte/value/NotKeywordError
  |~~ The value compared is a keyword. ~~|
  ::holds~(is ::keyword)

:keyword/gte/answer
  |~~ Whether the subject comes after the value compared or equals it. ~~|
  ::boolean

:keyword/lt
  |~~ Whether the subject's name precedes the name of the keyword the
      call gives.
  ~~|
  ::builtin{}

:keyword/lt/ordersByName
  |~~ `:a` precedes `:b`. ~~|
  ::law~(:a | lt :b | eq true)

:keyword/lt/value
  |~~ The value the subject is compared with. ~~|
  ~(/0)

:keyword/lt/value/NotKeywordError
  |~~ The value compared is a keyword. ~~|
  ::holds~(is ::keyword)

:keyword/lt/answer
  |~~ Whether the subject comes before the value compared. ~~|
  ::boolean

:keyword/lte
  |~~ Whether the subject's name precedes or equals the name of the
      keyword the call gives.
  ~~|
  ::builtin{}

:keyword/lte/holdsOfItself
  |~~ A keyword precedes or equals itself. ~~|
  ::law~(:a | lte :a | eq true)

:keyword/lte/value
  |~~ The value the subject is compared with. ~~|
  ~(/0)

:keyword/lte/value/NotKeywordError
  |~~ The value compared is a keyword. ~~|
  ::holds~(is ::keyword)

:keyword/lte/answer
  |~~ Whether the subject comes before the value compared or equals it. ~~|
  ::boolean

:keyword/keyword
  |~~ The name of the keyword, as a string: the reverse of `keyword` on
      a string, so `"foo" | keyword | keyword` answers `"foo"`.
  ~~|
  ::builtin{}

:keyword/keyword/answersTheName
  |~~ A keyword answers its name as a string. ~~|
  ::law~(:foo | keyword | eq "foo")

:keyword/keyword/keepsASpace
  |~~ A name with a space keeps it. ~~|
  ::law~(:"foo bar" | keyword | eq "foo bar")

:keyword/keyword/answer
  |~~ The name of the keyword, a string. ~~|
  ::string
